  "title": "Fed Rate Adjustments Amid Inflation Concerns and Global Supply Chain Disruptions",
  "summary": "The Federal Reserve faces potential rate hikes if inflation remains high, as Kevin Warsh warns, while Business Standard reports suggest inflation isn't slowing and interest rates are the central tool for achieving its mandate. The U.S. Federal Reserve faced mixed signals from recent July payrolls and job data, with weak figures providing some cover for its rate adjustments, while a disappointing job report left investors uncertain. Supply shocks to weaken monetary policy effectiveness: CEA V Anantha Nageswaran highlights the impact of global supply-side issues on inflation.",
